vision atlas
  Source   --feeds--> Encode  
  Encode   --feeds--> Package 
  Package  --feeds--> Serve   
  Serve    --feeds--> Play    
  Observe  --observes--> Play    
  Observe  --observes--> Source  
  Source   --governs--> Observe 
  Source    level=L1/family origin=environment
  Encode    level=L2/capability origin=environment
  Package   level=L3/contract origin=implementation
  Serve     level=L4/fixture origin=control
  Play      level=L5/trace origin=environment
  Observe   level=L6/receipt origin=evidence
gstreamer ontology
  states: NULL -> READY -> PAUSED -> PLAYING
  filesrc        L1/family      environment  serves=Source
    law:    the file opens and pushes buffers downstream
    hazard: the file opens and the pipeline stays PAUSED forever, never prerolling
  videotestsrc   L1/family      environment  serves=Source
    law:    a synthetic pattern is generated at the negotiated caps
    hazard: the pattern generates at caps nothing downstream can accept, and negotiation stalls
  udpsrc         L1/family      environment  serves=Source
    law:    datagrams arrive and become buffers with increasing timestamps
    hazard: the socket binds and no datagram ever arrives, which is indistinguishable from idle
  decodebin      L2/capability  environment  serves=Encode
    law:    a decoder is selected AND its dynamic pad is linked downstream
    hazard: the DYNAMIC pad is never linked, so no data flows and no error is ever posted — the classic GStreamer silent hang
  videoconvert   L2/capability  environment  serves=Encode
    law:    upstream caps are converted to something the encoder accepts
    hazard: conversion succeeds into caps the encoder then refuses, stalling negotiation
  x264enc        L2/capability  environment  serves=Encode
    law:    raw frames become an h264 elementary stream
    hazard: the encoder buffers input and emits nothing while the bus stays silent
  vp8enc         L2/capability  environment  serves=Encode
    law:    raw frames become a vp8 elementary stream
    hazard: the encoder runs at a bitrate that produces frames nothing can decode
  hlssink2       L3/contract    implementation serves=Package
    law:    a playlist is written naming segments that exist and are non-empty
    hazard: a playlist is written naming segments already deleted by the rolling window
  udpsink        L4/fixture     control      serves=Serve
    law:    packets leave the host toward the declared destination
    hazard: packets are sent to a black hole; udp gives no delivery signal at all
  appsink        L6/receipt     evidence     serves=Observe
    law:    buffers are handed to our code and are actually consumed
    hazard: buffers arrive with no callback attached and are silently dropped
vlc ontology (oracle, never author)
  play_url         L4/fixture     environment  serves=Serve
    law:    the URL opens and pictures are decoded from it
    hazard: VLC retries and buffers indefinitely on an unreachable URL rather than failing, so the run hangs instead of reporting
  play_file        L1/family      environment  serves=Source
    law:    the file opens and pictures are decoded from it
    hazard: a truncated file plays to Ended and reports no error at all
  sout_transcode   L2/capability  environment  serves=Encode
    law:    the transcode chain runs with the codecs that were declared
    hazard: an unavailable codec silently falls back, so the chain that ran is not the one declared
  sout_standard    L3/contract    environment  serves=Package
    law:    the output reaches the declared destination in the declared mux
    hazard: the destination is unreachable and output is discarded without a diagnostic
  snapshot         L6/receipt     evidence     serves=Observe
    law:    a decoded frame is written to disk and is non-empty
    hazard: a snapshot is written before the first frame decodes, producing a valid but BLANK image that compares as a real capture
  stats            L5/trace       evidence     serves=Play
    law:    decoded and lost picture counters are readable and advance
    hazard: the counters read zero both before playback starts and when it never starts
  leniencies (each hides a defect):
    skipped_frames       corrupt frames were dropped and playback continued, so a damaged stream looks watchable
    demuxer_fallback     a different demuxer was chosen than the container declared, so the format under test is not the format that was exercised
    codec_fallback       a software decoder replaced the expected one, so a hardware-path defect is invisible
    sout_stage_dropped   a missing stream-output module was skipped rather than refused, so the chain that ran is not the chain that was declared
    ended_without_error  playback reached Ended on input it could not fully read, so a truncated file reports the same terminal state as a whole one
obs ontology (compositor: loss is silent and the output stays continuous)
  scene_composite            L2/capability  environment  gl=true serves=Encode
    law:    the scene is drawn at the configured frame rate with every source visible
    hazard: the scene renders at a reduced rate and the output stays continuous, so loss is invisible without the counters
  source.media_file          L1/family      environment  gl=false serves=Source
    law:    the file decodes and its pictures appear in the composite
    hazard: the file ends and the source renders BLACK rather than stopping the scene
  source.display_capture     L1/family      environment  gl=true serves=Source
    law:    the screen's pixels reach the composite
    hazard: capture succeeds on a blanked or locked screen and yields black frames
  source.window_capture      L1/family      environment  gl=true serves=Source
    law:    the named window's pixels reach the composite
    hazard: the window is minimised or closed and the source renders BLACK while remaining 'active'
  source.video_device        L1/family      environment  gl=false serves=Source
    law:    the device opens and delivers frames at the negotiated format
    hazard: the device is held by another process and yields the last frame forever
  source.browser_source      L1/family      environment  gl=true serves=Source
    law:    the embedded page renders and its pixels reach the composite
    hazard: the page fails to load and renders transparent, compositing as nothing
  source.image_source        L1/family      environment  gl=false serves=Source
    law:    the still decodes and is drawn
    hazard: a missing file renders as an empty layer without a diagnostic
  output.stream_rtmp         L4/fixture     environment  gl=false serves=Serve
    law:    encoded frames are accepted by the ingest and acknowledged
    hazard: the ingest drops the connection and OBS RECONNECTS silently, so the output looks live through a gap
  output.record_file         L3/contract    implementation gl=false serves=Package
    law:    the file grows and its container is finalised on stop
    hazard: the process is killed rather than stopped, leaving an unfinalised container that most players still open
  output.virtual_camera      L4/fixture     environment  gl=false serves=Serve
    law:    the loopback device exists and other programs can open it
    hazard: the loopback module is absent and the output silently does nothing
  encoder_x264               L2/capability  environment  gl=false serves=Encode
    law:    frames are encoded within the frame budget, with none skipped
    hazard: the encoder falls behind and frames are SKIPPED before encoding, which the output stream cannot reveal
  stats_counters             L5/trace       evidence     gl=false serves=Observe
    law:    all three loss counters are readable
    hazard: the counters read zero before a run starts and after one that never began
  websocket_control          LX/control-plane control      gl=false serves=Play
    law:    a command is authenticated, applied, and its effect is observable
    hazard: a command is accepted and acknowledged without being applied
  loss counters:
    render_lag     environment  the compositor could not draw the scene in time — the GPU is the constraint
    encoding_lag   control      frames were SKIPPED before encoding because the encoder fell behind — the CPU budget is the constraint
    network_drop   environment  frames were encoded and then discarded because the output could not ship them — the link is the constraint
jmeter ontology (the measurement is about the generator until proven otherwise)
  thread_group                 L2/capability  environment    serves=Serve
    law:    the declared concurrency is actually reached and sustained
    hazard: the ramp-up is longer than the test, so the declared concurrency is never reached and the result describes a smaller load than the one reported
  http_sampler                 L4/fixture     environment    serves=Serve
    law:    each request is issued and its response fully read
    hazard: the response is counted before the body is read, so a server that stalls mid-body is recorded as fast
  assertion                    L3/contract    implementation serves=Package
    law:    the response BODY is checked, not merely its status code
    hazard: no assertion is attached, so every 200 passes — including an error page served with 200
  constant_throughput_timer    L2/capability  environment    serves=Serve
    law:    requests are issued on a schedule independent of how fast the server replies
    hazard: without pacing the client slows when the server does, hiding exactly the latency the test exists to find
  summary_report               L6/receipt     evidence       serves=Observe
    law:    percentiles are reported alongside the mean
    hazard: only the mean is read, so a server stalling one request in a hundred passes cleanly
  distributed_mode             LX/control-plane control        serves=Serve
    law:    every worker's clock and results are reconciled into one series
    hazard: one worker fails to start and the aggregate silently describes less load than intended
  contaminants (each makes a green report meaningless):
    no_assertion           a sampler passes on any HTTP 200, including a 200 carrying an error page, so '100% success' means only that the socket worked
    client_saturated       the generator's own CPU or connection pool was the limit, so the latency reported is the client queueing rather than the server responding
    coordinated_omission   an unpaced client sends FEWER requests when the server slows, so the slow responses are never issued and never measured — latency improves on paper as the server gets worse
    gui_mode               the GUI consumes the CPU it is measuring with, so the generator competes with its own measurement
    jvm_pause              a garbage-collection pause inside the generator is charged to the server, appearing as a response-time spike the server never caused
libav ontology (in-process: a failure here takes the harness with it)
  version_query          L0/product     environment    alloc=false unlock=false expires=false
    law:    the version reported is the LINKED library's, not a binary on PATH
    hazard: the header version and the linked version differ, so struct layouts disagree and fields are read at the wrong offsets
  open_input             L1/family      environment    alloc=true unlock=true expires=false
    law:    a context is allocated and the caller holds the obligation to close it
    hazard: the context is allocated and never closed, leaking memory the OCaml GC cannot see, so the process grows with no heap growth to explain it
  find_stream_info       L2/capability  environment    alloc=true unlock=true expires=false
    law:    stream parameters are populated before any decode is attempted
    hazard: it is skipped, and decode proceeds against uninitialised parameters that happen to be zero
  send_packet            L3/contract    implementation alloc=false unlock=true expires=false
    law:    a packet is accepted, or EAGAIN says the decoder must be drained first
    hazard: EAGAIN is treated as an error, aborting a decode that was working and only needed to be drained
  receive_frame          L3/contract    implementation alloc=true unlock=true expires=false
    law:    a frame is produced, or EAGAIN says more input is required
    hazard: any negative return is treated as failure, so a normal EAGAIN ends the loop and the file reports as undecodable
  frame_buffer_access    L6/receipt     implementation alloc=false unlock=false expires=false
    law:    pixels are read only while the frame reference is still held
    hazard: a Bigarray built over the frame ALIASES memory libav owns; after unref it is a live OCaml value pointing at freed memory, and the segfault lands somewhere unrelated
  unref_frame            L5/trace       implementation alloc=false unlock=false expires=true
    law:    the reference is dropped and every view onto it becomes unusable
    hazard: unref runs while a zero-copy view is still reachable from OCaml, which no type in the binding prevents unless it was designed to
  close_input            L1/family      implementation alloc=false unlock=false expires=true
    law:    the context is freed exactly once and no view outlives it
    hazard: the context is closed twice, or closed while frames derived from it are still held
  return codes: EAGAIN=-11 EOF=-541478725 — both negative, NEITHER a failure
browser video surface
  media_element      L3/contract    environment  serves=Play
    law:    a <video> element exists and exposes its media interface
    hazard: the element exists on every engine and decodes nothing without a codec
  codec_support      L3/contract    environment  serves=Play
    law:    the engine reports it can decode the codec we actually serve
    hazard: canPlayType returns the empty string for 'no', which is falsy but not absent
  frame_callback     L5/trace       evidence     serves=Play
    law:    a per-composited-frame callback fires and carries mediaTime
    hazard: the function exists and is never called because no frame is ever composited
  playback_quality   L5/trace       evidence     serves=Play
    law:    dropped and total frame counters are readable and advance
    hazard: the counters read zero both when playback is perfect and when it never began
  capture_stream     L6/receipt     evidence     serves=Observe
    law:    captureStream yields a live track carrying decoded video
    hazard: captureStream returns a stream whose video track list is empty
  media_recorder     L6/receipt     evidence     serves=Observe
    law:    MediaRecorder accepts that track and emits non-empty blobs
    hazard: recording starts and every dataavailable blob has size zero
  media_source       L4/fixture     environment  serves=Play
    law:    MediaSource accepts a SourceBuffer for our mime and codec
    hazard: MediaSource exists but isTypeSupported is false for the codec we serve
  web_codecs         L5/trace       environment  serves=Observe
    law:    VideoDecoder is configurable for the codec and emits VideoFrames
    hazard: VideoDecoder constructs and configure() rejects asynchronously
  web_rtc            L4/fixture     environment  serves=Play
    law:    an RTCPeerConnection can be constructed and negotiate a video track
    hazard: the peer connection constructs and never negotiates a media section
  universal codecs: vp9, av1
