STPA: 16 unsafe control actions, 0 with NOTHING enforcing the constraint
  restart            not_provided       enforced
    when: the running image differs from the built one and the pipeline is degraded
    then: the old image serves indefinitely and the fix never reaches production
    must: a digest change must eventually produce a restart
    by:   Vision_restart.supervise_once (digest compared each tick)
  restart            provided_unsafe    enforced
    when: the replacement image is broken
    then: the service is taken down and cannot come back
    must: the old instance must not be retired until the replacement passes a health gate
    by:   Vision_restart.execute (law 1, chaos-tested over 7 failure modes)
  restart            wrong_timing       enforced
    when: in-flight segment requests have not finished
    then: viewers see refused connections mid-stream
    must: accepting must stop and in-flight responses must finish before the swap
    by:   Vision_restart.execute (Draining precedes Starting)
  restart            stopped_too_soon   enforced
    when: the gate ran before the replacement had opened its listener
    then: a healthy replacement is rolled back, or a broken one is promoted
    must: the gate must ask what the stage probes ask, not whether the process exists
    by:   Vision_control (ffmpeg gate is probe_package; server gate polls /whoami)
  start_pipeline     provided_unsafe    enforced
    when: a pipeline is already running against the same output directory
    then: two encoders write one playlist and the stream becomes undecodable
    must: starting must be refused while another pipeline owns the output
    by:   Vision_controller.start (lock_holder checked BEFORE the spawn)
  start_pipeline     not_provided       enforced
    when: the pipeline has died and nothing restarts it
    then: the stream ends silently while the server keeps serving a stale playlist
    must: a dead pipeline must be detected and reported
    by:   Vision_controller.probe_source (Absent when the process exited)
  stop_pipeline      stopped_too_soon   enforced
    when: SIGKILL before the muxer finalises
    then: an unfinalised container that most players still open, so corruption is invisible
    must: stopping must send SIGTERM and wait before escalating
    by:   Vision_controller.stop (TERM, settle, then KILL)
  stop_pipeline      wrong_timing       enforced
    when: stop is issued while a capture is being compared
    then: the comparison reads a truncated capture and reports a false divergence
    must: a capture in progress must complete or be discarded, never half-read
    by:   Vision_serve POST /capture (reads to Content-Length; a short read is a 500 and nothing is written)
  start_pipeline     wrong_timing       enforced
    when: started before the output directory exists or is writable
    then: ffmpeg exits immediately and the failure looks like a bad intent
    must: the sink must be created and writable before the process is spawned
    by:   Vision_controller.start (mkdir_p before create_process)
  start_pipeline     stopped_too_soon   enforced
    when: probed before the first segment boundary
    then: a healthy pipeline reports Unknown and is treated as broken
    must: a pipeline must be given time to reach its first segment before judgement
    by:   Vision_controller.probe_package (Unknown, not Absent, before the playlist)
  stop_pipeline      not_provided       enforced
    when: a run ends without stopping the pipeline it started
    then: an orphan ffmpeg holds the output directory and corrupts the next run
    must: every started pipeline must be stopped on every exit path
    by:   Vision_controller (at_exit walks started_pipelines)
  stop_pipeline      provided_unsafe    enforced
    when: stop is issued to a pid that has been reused by another process
    then: an unrelated process is killed
    must: a pid must be validated as ours before a signal is sent to it
    by:   Vision_controller.stop_pid (owns_pid gates every signal)
  publish_telemetry  not_provided       enforced
    when: the router is unreachable
    then: the mesh view is incomplete and looks the same as a healthy quiet system
    must: an unpublished observation must be counted and disclosed
    by:   Vision_telemetry.render (reports 'mesh view incomplete')
  publish_telemetry  provided_unsafe    enforced
    when: a payload carries a credential or a private path
    then: secrets are broadcast to every subscriber on the mesh
    must: published payloads must contain only observations, never configuration
    by:   Vision_telemetry.redact (applied to every payload before it goes out)
  publish_telemetry  wrong_timing       enforced
    when: published before the probe completed
    then: a verdict is broadcast that the probe later contradicts
    must: telemetry must be published from a completed observation
    by:   Vision_run (publishes after probe_all returns)
  publish_telemetry  stopped_too_soon   enforced
    when: the run exits before the last observation is flushed
    then: the mesh's last view of a failing run is a healthy one
    must: the terminal observation must be published before exit
    by:   Vision_telemetry (at_exit warns when a run published and never closed)

